#: src/Admin/AdminMenu.php:286
msgid "Which axis should carry your workflow?"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/AdminMenu.php:289
msgid "If your workflow is about getting the goods out — made, packed, booked, shipped — put it on the shipping status. FluentCart never writes that column by itself, and its own “Change Shipping Status” dialog lists your custom steps directly. The order status is the other way round: FluentCart rewrites it to “Processing” whenever a payment lands, and its admin has no control for choosing an order status at all — only fixed buttons such as Mark As Complete and Cancel Order — so this plugin supplies both the guard and the control."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/AdminMenu.php:293
msgid "Create the fulfilment workflow (shipping axis)"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/AdminMenu.php:294
msgid "Adds the shipping statuses “In production” and “Shipment scheduled” between the built-in Unshipped and Shipped. FluentCart’s built-in statuses keep their own names, and nothing you have already set up is overwritten."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/AdminMenu.php:297
msgid "The order-axis version of the same workflow is on the Order statuses tab. Use it when the states you need really are states of the order rather than of the delivery — “awaiting artwork approval”, say — or when you want them on the status your customers already see."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/AdminMenu.php:300
#: src/Admin/OrderWidget.php:146
msgid "Order workflow"
